# A toggle in GMS with no wait behind it, so an archer holds it forever: what
# it really is, is an attack on a clock of its own.
#
# 400 + 16x% on one enemy, and GMS's `nbdR` of 20% against anything that is
# not a boss -- a share of the archer's damage, not points on the arrow.
#
# GMS states no rate for it anywhere a player can read. The invisible half of
# the skill carries 90 strikes over the 60 seconds it stands for, which is one
# every two thirds of a second; the user timed a video and agreed. That is 22
# ticks, so it lands square on the clock.
name: "Guided Arrow"
description: "Creates spirit arrows that pursue and attack nearby enemies."
kind: SKILL_KIND_AUTO_ATTACK
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_BOW_MASTER_V skill_order: 2 }
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_MARKSMAN_V skill_order: 2 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_ARCHETYPE
max_level: 30
max_enemies: 1
cast_interval_seconds: 0.66
base {
  skill_pct: 4.16
  normal_pct: 0.20
}
per_level { skill_pct: 0.16 }
